        "source_message_id": 42,
        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "Hi,\n\n[FREELANCER_NAME_002] you for providing [FREELANCER_NAME_006] revised report design. [FREELANCER_NAME_006] overall direction has improved considerably, and I’m satisfied with [FREELANCER_NAME_006] general appearance and style. I therefore do not want [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report redesigned from [FREELANCER_NAME_006] beginning.\n\nBefore approving it, I’d like one final refinement round focused on readability, consistency, and a stronger overall commercial finish.\n\n[FREELANCER_NAME_006] requested updates are:\n\n1. Give [FREELANCER_NAME_006] front-page score greater prominence.\n\nPlease enlarge [FREELANCER_NAME_006] \"22/100\" score slightly and add more space around it so that it functions as [FREELANCER_NAME_006] main dashboard result. On opening [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report, [FREELANCER_NAME_006] customer should immediately see both [FREELANCER_NAME_006] score and [FREELANCER_NAME_006] risk outcome.\n\n2. Change \"Security Score\" to \"Vehicle Security Score\"\n\nPlease replace [FREELANCER_NAME_006] front-page heading \"Security Score\" with \"Vehicle Security Score\" so [FREELANCER_NAME_006] wording appears more complete and professional.\n\n3. Streamline [FREELANCER_NAME_006] \"What Caused This Result\" section.\n\nAlthough [FREELANCER_NAME_006] wording is good, [FREELANCER_NAME_006] dark blue panel currently contains too much text. Please convert it into shorter bullet points that are easier to scan, for example:\n\n- No independent immobilisation\n- No circular steering lock\n- No live-location tracking\n- Storage location is being overvalued\n- Owner security habits reduce protection\n\nIf necessary, [FREELANCER_NAME_006] more detailed explanation can stay elsewhere in [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report. However, page one needs to be quicker and easier to read.\n\n4. Delete placeholder text\n\nPlease remove placeholders such as \"Click to enter a date.\" Replace this with [FREELANCER_NAME_006] actual assessment date or use a clean editable placeholder such as \"\\[Assessment Date\\]\".\n\n5. Verify [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report code throughout\n\nPlease ensure [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report code is used consistently in every location. I noticed that certain sections may contain \"PR-01\". Unless there is a specific reason to use another code, it should read \"RR-01\" throughout.\n\n6. Improve [FREELANCER_NAME_006] vehicle group section\n\nUsing checkboxes beside Range Rover / Range Rover Sport / Defender makes this area look more like an uncompleted form than a finished report. Please either present it as a cleaner fixed line, such as:\n\n\"Vehicle Group: Range Rover / Range Rover Sport / Defender\"\n\nor tailor it to [FREELANCER_NAME_006] customer, for example:\n\n\"Vehicle Assessed: Range Rover Sport\"\n\n7. Include a discreet header from pages 2 onwards\n\n[FREELANCER_NAME_006] footer is working well, but for consistency I’d also like [FREELANCER_NAME_006] internal pages to carry a subtle header. A simple option would be:\n\n\"Vehicle Theft Risk Assessment | RR-01 | Confidential\"\n\nIt should remain understated and use very little space.\n\n8. Make [FREELANCER_NAME_006] red distribution warning on [FREELANCER_NAME_006] final page more refined\n\nI’m happy with [FREELANCER_NAME_006] concept of [FREELANCER_NAME_006] warning section, but [FREELANCER_NAME_006] current red block is visually too heavy. Please retain [FREELANCER_NAME_006] warning while reducing its dominance and refining its appearance, ensuring it still clearly states that [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report is confidential and intended for limited distribution.\n\nIn general, I’m pleased with [FREELANCER_NAME_006] design direction. This final round should concentrate on polish, readability, consistency, and ensuring [FREELANCER_NAME_006] report presents as a premium paid assessment.\n\nPlease confirm whether these instructions are clear and advise when you expect to provide [FREELANCER_NAME_006] revised version.\n\nThanks"
